13.8 Reviewer Independence

Independent reviewers should, where practical, have sufficient access to the relevant research artefacts to examine:

- architecture definitions;
- assumptions;
- scenario configurations;
- source-code versions;
- experimental procedures;
- test results;
- audit records;
- limitations;
- and conclusions.

Review independence should be preserved wherever reasonably possible.

The objective of independent review is to expose weaknesses, inconsistencies or unsupported assumptions.

---

13.9 Review Findings

Future review findings should be classified according to their nature.

Possible classifications include:

- observation;
- recommendation;
- clarification required;
- minor deficiency;
- major deficiency;
- unresolved issue;
- research limitation;
- validation gap;
- software defect;
- modelling limitation;
- or closed finding.

Each significant finding should, where practical, include:

FINDING → IMPACT → RESPONSE → CORRECTIVE ACTION → VERIFICATION → CLOSURE

Open findings should remain visible until appropriately resolved or formally accepted as limitations.

---

